# Generated by `wrangler types`, and NOT reproducible across machines: it
# inlines whatever `vars` your .env happens to define, and it gains a
# `mainModule` entry only once a build output exists. Tracking it meant a
# developer's local secret NAMES landed in the repo, and `wrangler types --check`
# failed for anyone whose .env differed. Regenerated by `prepare` and by CI.
worker-configuration.d.ts

# Test output. None of it has ever been committed, but `git add -A` after an E2E
# run would sweep a report in, and a 40MB trace in history is not removable.
playwright-report
blob-report
coverage
